) $3,000 for the medical care of H; (
b
) $2,000 for the medical care of W; and (
c
) $3,000 for the medical care of the dependent child. No part of these payments was for medicine and drugs nor compensated for by insurance or otherwise. The allowable deduction under section 213 for medical expenses paid in 1956 is $6,800 computed as follows:

